From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:03:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(web): each jstack tree menu item carries the action
 it runs

A row's menu is built beside the row, each item with its own run, so the
shared id union of jstackRowMenu and the row.kind guards that re-checked it
go: an item can no longer be paired with another row's action. The menu
still crosses to the desktop process as data, by each item's place.

A browser test opens every row kind's menu (a project with a home and one
without, a home, a worker, a queued and an asking task, and "more") and
picks every item, asserting it runs that item's action and no other.
